   "platform-product/source/c28da7d5203f7a409e77b95a4f5586469dc4eec50620e92326f40fa19110fa9a",
   :added-current-work-text
   ". DOM1 acceptance requires fixed synthesis-visible shapes, finite iteration and explicit CDC synchronizer/FIFO/handshake, proof or audit waiver; reject implicit widths/truncation, unsafe CDC, runtime-only constructs and nonfinite loops. Emit HDL, interface/clock/reset/timing records, source maps, testbench and simulation evidence. Exercise FIFO full/empty/reset/backpressure/data order plus counter and bus-peripheral fixtures. Dependencies: profile legality, HDL lowering, no-runtime and safety/proof consumers; target choice remains open ; P8 target conformance requires fixed-width shape/overflow checks, static unroll or structural conversion or rejection, explicit input-only nondeterminism, state-graph emission AND validation (initial/reset/transition/output/illegal-state behavior), clock/reset records (explicit uninitialized state allowed; unsafe power-on needs hardware audit), ports/protocols and CDC synchronizer/FIFO/handshake/proof or audited waiver. Reject runtime services and unmediated CDC. Capability targets must validate bounds/provenance/permissions/sealing/derivation, tags across register/memory/DMA/FIFO/bus/debug/port paths, declared compartment entry/return/shared-state authority and explicit temporal assumptions. Tag-destroying paths are marked and diagnosed unless source explicitly expects destruction; audited authority boundaries retain their conditions. A conforming target may declare no temporal revocation; stronger source requirements then reject or require separate proof. Emit source-mapped hardware IR/HDL, target/layout/tag/clock/reset/timing/port/compartment reports and positive/negative capability-target fixtures. ISA/product/fabrication selection remains unassessed. Criterion profile-gap/domain/hardware-cdc (Open): Input: Typed P8/DOM1 hardware graph with declared source/destination clocks and every cross-clock signal, port, bus or state edge. Accept: Associate each crossing with an explicit synchronizer, asynchronous FIFO, handshake, Gray-coded/equivalent proof or external hardware CDC waiver with audit record; validate the declared mediator and retain its source/proof/audit identity through hardware IR and HDL. Reject: Unmediated or unproven crossing, missing/incompatible clock-domain evidence and runtime synchronization substituted for hardware semantics. Required outputs: CDC graph/report, accepted synchronizer/FIFO/handshake fixtures and rejected unsafe crossing diagnostic with module/signal/state/span/clock/reset/HDL/missing-proof/remediation; preserve simulation, HDL source maps and conformance evidence from the DOM1 consumer. Dependencies: backend-hdl, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping domain/hardware-cdc; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/hardware/capability-representation (Open): Input: Capability-hardware target manifest and typed pointer operation with word/address widths, bounds/granularity, provenance/derivation, permission bits, tag/seal/object/entry metadata. Accept: Select hardware capabilities only through the target manifest; type/layout-check representation and derivations for preserved provenance, enforced bounds and non-widening permissions. A conditional audited hardware authority boundary must retain its explicit preconditions and evidence. Reject: Pointers treated as integers, fabricated provenance, undeclared integer round-trip, unsupported representation or unchecked bounds/permission widening. Required outputs: Capability pointer/layout/metadata target manifest, legal derivation and rejected widening/representation fixtures, P8-CAPABILITY diagnostics identifying metadata field, module/signal/origin and target evidence. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types2-check-declared-abstractions, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, backend-hdl interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping hardware/capability-representation; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/hardware/capability-tag-paths (Open): Input: Every capability-bearing register, memory, DMA, FIFO, bus/bridge, debug and external-port path with target tag/metadata propagation or destruction declaration. Accept: Preserve tags and capability metadata on all declared carrying paths, or mark a tag-destroying boundary and diagnose unless source explicitly expects destruction; retain audited authority-boundary qualifications. Reject: Unmarked tag/metadata loss, silent ordinary-storage conversion and omitted path/target support evidence; explicit expected destruction is a qualified legal test case rather than an unconditional rejection. Required outputs: Tag-preservation/path report and capability-bearing interface manifests; preserving, marked-destruction, explicitly-expected-destruction and unmarked-loss fixtures with P8-TAG path/origin/target context. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types2-check-declared-abstractions, lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs, backend-hdl interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping hardware/capability-tag-paths; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/hardware/clock-reset-contract (Open): Input: Hardware registers/state with clock domain and reset sync/async, active level, value and affected-register declarations. Accept: Assign each register a domain and defined reset or explicitly uninitialized state; require a hardware audit for unsafe/unspecified power-on behavior and preserve the accepted declaration into clock/reset/timing records. Reject: Missing/invalid domain or reset, undeclared power-on behavior and lost initialization evidence. Required outputs: Clock/reset-domain and initialization reports, accepted declared-uninitialized/audited-power-on cases, rejected missing-clock/reset cases and P8-CLOCK/RESET diagnostics. Dependencies: legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, backend-hdl interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping hardware/clock-reset-contract; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/hardware/compartment-boundary (Open): Input: Capability-hardware compartment crossing with compartment IDs, sealed entry/call gates, call/return authority, bounded shared state and transferred-capability lifetime/revocation assumptions. Accept: Validate the explicit authority transfer, legal entry and return paths and permitted sharing/lifetime assumptions at each crossing. Reject: Implicit sharing through wires/debug/untyped maps, undeclared entry or return authority, invalid sealed state and omitted shared-memory/lifetime rules. Required outputs: Compartment/authority-transfer and temporal-assumption report, sealed-entry/call/return/shared-state positive/negative cases and P8-COMPARTMENT boundary/origin/metadata diagnostics. Dependencies: legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, backend-hdl interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn