uctural-profile-contract; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/hardware/temporal-protection (Open): Input: Capability target's declared hardware/allocator/compiler revocation, epoch/quarantine, static-lifetime or explicitly absent temporal protection and the source's required protection. Accept: Record actual temporal assumptions independently of spatial bounds; admit a conforming no-revocation target where source does not require stronger protection, or consume a separate valid proof satisfying the stronger requirement. Reject: Temporal protection inferred from spatial bounds, omitted temporal assumptions and stronger use-after-free requirements unsupported by the actual target or separate proof. Required outputs: Temporal/compartment assumption manifest, no-revocation acceptance and stronger-required rejection/proof cases, P8-TEMPORAL diagnostic identifying failed assumption and origin. Dependencies: legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, backend-hdl interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping hardware/temporal-protection; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. For this target, the architecture owner records the concrete target/ABI, accepted artifact kind, named simulator/device evidence and required service set before implementation scope is claimed. Reject a scope claim missing any required selection or incompatible with the declared profile; no target or product is selected by this task. Target integration consumes the exact Lower/Emit artifact and explicit runtime or no-runtime manifest plus required standard-library adapters. Record actual simulation/execution and applicable layout, clock, interrupt, unsafe-island, grant and sou