   ". DOM3 acceptance requires typed syscall/user-pointer taint, capability and error mapping; raw-memory safe-wrapper/audit, allocation/panic/preemption/interrupt and ABI records. Exercise valid/invalid syscall, interrupt, allocator and page-table cases, reject ambient authority and hosted assumptions, and emit kernel object/boot image, syscall/interrupt tables, audit/capability/source maps and named emulator smoke evidence. Dependencies: profile legality, native lowering, ownership and runtime/FFI boundaries; OS product architecture remains unadopted ; P7 target conformance requires explicit page/frame/pinned/address-space/DMA and interrupt-safe allocator/failure/concurrency policy; reject hidden allocation/hosted services and unsupported atomics/fences. Check interrupt reentrancy/shared state/stack/latency/effects and scheduler block/sleep/preempt/allocate/context/lock rules; reject blocking in invalid lock or interrupt context. Driver ABI/device/grant/buffer/DMA/callback/error/unsafe-wrapper records retain provenance; actual device transfer and callback entry are separate Runtime/Devices consumers. Emit capability/memory/device/interrupt/scheduler/atomic/ABI/unsafe/no-hidden-allocation evidence. OS architecture/product selection remains unassessed. Criterion profile-gap/kernel/driver-boundary (Open): Input: Kernel driver ABI and device map with grants, buffer ownership, DMA synchronization, interrupt/callback rules, typed status/errors and audited unsafe wrappers. Accept: Validate the declaration and ABI independently of actual DMA/device transfer and callback entry; preserve device/ABI provenance in generated bindings, enforce ownership/coherency/synchronization and re-entry rules at their consuming boundaries. Reject: Incomplete ABI/device/authority, invalid buffer lifetime or DMA order, unsafe callback entry, untyped host failure and raw operations outside reviewed wrappers. Required outputs: Driver ABI/device/capability/unsafe manifests and executed declaration/transfer/callback positive/negative fixtures with P7-ABI/MMIO/AUTHORITY or boundary-specific context. Dependencies: devices, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping kernel/driver-boundary; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/kernel/interrupt-scheduling-contract (Open): Input: Kernel handler/vector and scheduler/lock operations with priority, stack, latency, allowed effects/shared state, atomic/lock/reentrancy/preemption and block/sleep/allocate/context policy. Accept: Check handler context separately from scheduler/lock transitions; preserve declared no-alloc and interrupt-safe operations, supported atomics/fences and the required physical stack/latency evidence. Reject: Blocking/sleeping under invalid locks or in interrupt handlers, hidden allocation/host services, unsupported atomic/fence context and missing required reentrancy/shared-state/stack/latency declarations. Required outputs: Interrupt/scheduler/atomic support and safety reports, no-allocation and legal/illegal lock/preempt/block fixtures, P7-INTERRUPT/SCHEDULER/ATOMIC diagnostics with subsystem/region/origin/context. Dependencies: devices, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping kernel/interrupt-scheduling-contract; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/kernel/profile-memory-contract (Open): Input: Kernel memory/provider and privileged-facility declarations with page/frame ownership, pinning, address spaces, DMA, allocator failure/concurrency, region/arena and interrupt-safe policy. Accept: Validate memory-regime/allocation legality separately from effect/capability admission of raw memory/MMIO/interrupt/scheduler/register operations; no-alloc functions emit no allocation effects and selected services remain explicit. Reject: Hidden allocation, GC/hosted/runtime assumptions, reflection/eval/ambient host services/model/tool calls, unbounded exceptions unless explicitly modeled, and ungranted privileged operations. Required outputs: Kernel profile/capability/memory/map/allocator/no-hidden-allocation and unsafe reports, legal provider fixtures and P7-HIDDEN-ALLOC/GC/RAW-MEMORY/EXCEPTION/AUTHORITY diagnostics. Dependencies: legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping kernel/profile-memory-contract; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. For this target, the architecture owner records the concrete target/ABI, accepted artifact kind, named simulator/device evidence and required service set before implementation scope is claimed. Reject a scope claim missing any required selection or incompatible with the declared profile; no target or product is selected by this task. Target integration consumes the exact Lower/Emit artifact and explicit runtime or no-runtime manifest plus required standard-library adapters. Record actual simulation/execution and applicable layout, clock, interrupt, unsafe-island, grant and source-to-artifact provenance checks; reject forbidden services, missing adapters, unauditable authority or a record-only execution claim. These target gates do not require completion of the full Platform Product.. Criterion `domain/kernel-artifact-production`: Produce source-linked kernel artifact, unsafe audit/capability manifests and emulator smoke evidence for the declared kernel slice. Accepted fixture: Emit the declared kernel object/boot image with syscall/interrupt tables, ABI, unsafe-audit, capability and source/debug maps. Negative fixture: Reject missing audit/provenance or claims lacking named emulator smoke evidence. Required evidence: kernel artifact pack and emulator smoke report; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume backend-llvm, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-ownership-borrow-initialization-and-lifetime-analysis outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed. Criterion `domain/kernel-syscall-integration`: Execute the declared typed syscall on the named emulator/substrate with accepted/rejected authority and memory-boundary cases. Accepted fixture: Invoke the typed syscall on the named emulator/substrate with user-pointer taint, raw wrapper/bounds, authority, context and error mapping. Negative fixture: Reject unauthorized or invalid user-memory input and hosted runtime assumptions. Required evidence: syscall table, valid/invalid invocation trace and denial diagnostics; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume backend-llvm, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-ownership-borrow-initialization-and-lifetime-analysis outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed. Criterion `domain/kernel-user-boundary`: Enforce typed syscall/user-kernel input, taint, capability and error contracts with audited privileged implementation boundaries. Accepted fixture: Enforce declared syscall schemas, user-pointer validation/taint, capabilities and error translation through audited privileged wrappers. Negative fixture: Reject schema-less/taint-unsafe entry, unaudited raw memory and ambient authority. Required evidence: kernel ABI/syscall schema, wrapper audit and boundary fixtures; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume backend-llvm, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-ownership-borrow-initialization-and-lifetime-analysis outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed.",
